meta {
  name: 08 - Archival Capability Matrix
  type: graphql
  seq: 8
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}
  body: graphql
  auth: inherit
}

body:graphql {
  query ArchivalCapabilityMatrix {
    IssueFilter: __type(name: "IssueFilter") { inputFields { name } }
    ProjectFilter: __type(name: "ProjectFilter") { inputFields { name } }
    InitiativeFilter: __type(name: "InitiativeFilter") { inputFields { name } }
    IssueLabelFilter: __type(name: "IssueLabelFilter") { inputFields { name } }
    IssueSortInput: __type(name: "IssueSortInput") { inputFields { name } }
  }
}

docs {
  Reference: https://linear.app/developers/filtering

  **This request exists because `14 - Issues Include Archived` came back a VERIFIED
  NEGATIVE: archiving a record does NOT bump its `updatedAt`.** (Confirmed 2026-08-04 by
  `Seeding/D2` — EST-2's `updatedAt` stayed at `2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z` while
  `archivedAt` became `2026-08-04T18:13:09.393Z`.) An `updatedAt`-cursored sweep can
  therefore never re-emit an archived row, and `includeArchived: true` buys incremental
  sync nothing on its own. The only remaining incremental route to archival is a filter on
  `archivedAt` itself — so this probe asks which filter types actually offer one.

  **Limitation / observed finding** (confirmed 2026-08-04): the capability is NOT uniform
  across the cluster. This asymmetry is the cluster's real fault line — deletion-capture
  capability, not ordering.

  | filter type | `archivedAt` filterable? |
  |---|---|
  | `IssueFilter` | **YES** |
  | `ProjectFilter` | **NO** |
  | `InitiativeFilter` | **NO** |
  | `IssueLabelFilter` | **NO** |

  Passing it anyway to the three that lack it fails loudly, e.g.
  `Field "archivedAt" is not defined by type "ProjectFilter"`.

  **`IssueSortInput` also has NO `archivedAt` member** (verified here; the members are
  priority, estimate, title, label, labelGroup, slaStatus, createdAt, updatedAt,
  completedAt, dueDate, accumulatedStateUpdatedAt, cycle, milestone, assignee, delegate,
  project, team, manual, workflowState, customer, customerRevenue, customerCount,
  customerImportantCount, rootIssue, linkCount, release). So Issues' archival pass can
  FILTER on `archivedAt` but cannot SORT by it — which forces that pass onto end-of-sweep
  checkpointing, the same policy Labels needs for its `updatedAt` sweep. See
  `15 - Issues Archival Sweep`.

  Consequence: Issues can capture archival incrementally; Projects, Initiatives and Labels
  cannot, by any available filter.

  **Resolution (reviewed decision, 2026-08-13):** accepted as an explicit connector
  limitation. Projects / Initiatives / Labels stay incremental+backfill, and the connector's
  user-facing docs must state that archival and deletion of those three are NOT captured —
  an archived record remains in the destination indefinitely with `archivedAt: null`,
  indistinguishable from a live one, until a full backfill reconciles it.

  Snapshot reclassification (which would infer deletions natively) and a scheduled full
  refresh were both considered and declined in favor of keeping the `updatedAt` cursor and
  the low steady-state request cost. Snapshotting remains the cheap upgrade path if the
  limitation bites: the shared connection walk already produces what a `fetch_snapshot`
  needs, so it is a resource-registration change rather than new fetch logic. Labels and
  Initiatives are the natural first candidates.
}


example {
  name: 200 — archivedAt filterable on IssueFilter ONLY

  request: {
    url: https://api.linear.app/graphql
    method: POST
    mode: graphql

    body:graphql: {
      query ArchivalCapabilityMatrix {
        IssueFilter: __type(name: "IssueFilter") { inputFields { name } }
        ProjectFilter: __type(name: "ProjectFilter") { inputFields { name } }
        InitiativeFilter: __type(name: "InitiativeFilter") { inputFields { name } }
        IssueLabelFilter: __type(name: "IssueLabelFilter") { inputFields { name } }
        IssueSortInput: __type(name: "IssueSortInput") { inputFields { name } }
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    headers: {
      x-complexity: 11
      x-ratelimit-requests-limit: 2500
      x-ratelimit-requests-remaining: 2492
      x-ratelimit-complexity-limit: 3000000
      x-ratelimit-complexity-remaining: 2999989
    }

    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }

    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "IssueFilter": {
              "has_archivedAt": true
            },
            "ProjectFilter": {
              "has_archivedAt": false
            },
            "InitiativeFilter": {
              "has_archivedAt": false
            },
            "IssueLabelFilter": {
              "has_archivedAt": false
            },
            "IssueSortInput": {
              "has_archivedAt": false
            }
          }
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
